Package: rwarp
Title: Plannable Raster Warp via Rust (rwarp)
Version: 0.1.0.9000
Authors@R:
    person("Michael", "Sumner", , "mdsumner@gmail.com", role = c("aut", "cre"))
Description: Provides R bindings to the rwarp Rust crate: a GDAL-style raster
    warp pipeline implemented in pure Rust using the proj crate for coordinate
    transforms. The package exposes a plannable, inspectable warp workflow where
    the chunk plan (source windows, fill ratios) can be examined before
    execution, and the read function is user-swappable (GDAL, byte-ref COG,
    Zarr). Core functions replace vapour::gdal_raster_data() and related
    gdal_raster_* utilities for common reprojection tasks.
License: MIT + file LICENSE
Encoding: UTF-8
Roxygen: list(markdown = TRUE)
SystemRequirements: Cargo (Rust's package manager), rustc (>= 1.86),
    PROJ (>= 9.6.2), pkg-config
